<title>USA: Nickles - tobacco ad curbs should be by law, not reg.</title>
<headline>Nickles - tobacco ad curbs should be by law, not reg.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Restrictions on tobacco-related advertising should be done through the legislative process not by regulation, Assistant Senate Majority Leader Don Nickles (R-Okla.) said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Regulations restricting advertising and promotion of tobacco products aimed at young people are to go into effect next year.</p>
<p>&quot;If we're going to have significant policy change, it should be done through the legislative process - it shouldn't be done by (FDA Administrator David) Kessler, who's leaving,&quot; he told a National Association of Manufacturers' breakfast. &quot;Congress should vote on it.&quot;</p>
</text>
